Walcher's work in the metalworkers' union brings a few local posts and a better hearing. The union bureaucracy answers with expulsions wherever it can.

@factory_councils
title: Build factory-council networks
subtitle: Link the factory councils across districts. · dev: workers_kpd +2×m, kf_centre_strength +2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if walcher_timer > 0 : [+ walcher_timer +] months before this adviser can act again. ?]
choose-if: walcher_timer = 0
on-arrival: walcher_timer = 3; workers_kpd += 2*campaign_mult; kf_centre_strength += 2

The factory councils begin to coordinate across districts. They are the closest thing we have to an organization of workers' power, and also the first thing the authorities will try to break.
